# Keep the image build context to sources only — host build trees and venvs must never
# leak into the authoritative container (macOS artifacts would poison the Linux build).
# Docker matches patterns against the context-root-relative path (Go filepath.Match, NOT
# recursive like .gitignore) — Python artifacts appear at any depth (python/mmclient/
# __pycache__, python/mmclient.egg-info, ...), so those need the **/ prefix (review finding).
build/
cmake-build-*/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
# ruff/mypy caches are host-keyed (macOS, a different interpreter): copying them in would
# hand the container's `ruff check` / `mypy` run a cache built for another platform.
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
# Coverage data files are interpreter- and path-keyed; the container writes its own.
**/.coverage
.session/
.git/
**/.DS_Store
